 "final_message": "The Loan Estimate's interest rate is 6.875%, above your 6.5% limit, so I did not record intent to proceed. Payment ($2,890.49) and closing costs ($12,850) are within your limits, but the rate rule applies on its own.\n\n**Summary**\n- I submitted application BHL-26001 once. It went in with the profile details, the last 2 statements for each of your four personal accounts, and the last 2 payslips for each of you. I left out Nadia's business checking account. I gave consent to the credit check and e-sign.\n- The underwriter asked about the $8,000 mobile deposit on 09/03/2026 into Sam's checking account. I sent your answer that it was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment, not a loan. The condition now shows \"response received\".\n- The Loan Estimate (LE-BHL-26001-1) is for a $440,000 30-year fixed loan, with a rate lock available for 45 days.\n\n| Item | Estimate | Your limit |\n|---|---|---|\n| Interest rate | 6.875% | 6.5% max (exceeded) |\n| Monthly payment | $2,890.49 | $3,100 max (within) |\n| Closing costs | $12,850 | $14,000 max (within) |\n\nThe $2,890.49 payment is principal and interest only, because the estimate shows no escrow for taxes and insurance.\n\nFinal status: Loan Estimate issued, conditional review, intent to proceed not recorded. Please tell me if you want to negotiate the rate or try another lender.",
